{# Record continuity of this run's route.

   How much of the intended record exists, from the route's first run up to
   this one: the sealed runs, how complete they were, and the runs the
   schedule expects. Continuity says nothing about condition, and the section
   says so. Seals and the chain are reported beside it, as separate claims.

   With no continuity there is no score, and the section says why rather
   than leaving itself out. #}
<section class="section continuity" id="continuity">

  <h2>Record continuity</h2>

  {% if continuity %}
    <p class="lede">
      Continuity is how much of the intended record exists for this route: the
      sealed runs, times how complete they were, out of the runs the schedule
      expects. It says nothing about condition. A route where every scheduled
      run was sealed and every checkpoint failed has 100% continuity.
    </p>

    <p class="lede">
      The window runs from the route's first run to this run's date. Only the
      runs before this one are counted: this run is sealed from this report,
      so it has no seal yet.
    </p>

    {% set days = continuity_days %}
    {% set per_day = (continuity.runs_expected // days) if days else 0 %}
    <table class="data-table continuity-score">
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Route</td>
          <td>{{ continuity.route_id }}</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Window</td>
          <td>
            {{ continuity.window.from }} to {{ continuity.window.to }}
            <span class="row-id">{{ days }} day{{ "" if days == 1 else "s" }}</span>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Runs expected</td>
          <td>
            {{ continuity.runs_expected }}
            <span class="row-id">{{ per_day }} a day for {{ days }} day{{ "" if days == 1 else "s" }}</span>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Runs completed</td>
          <td>
            {{ continuity.runs_completed }}
            <span class="row-id">Runs in the window with a seal</span>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Coverage mean</td>
          <td>
            {{ continuity.coverage_mean | show("no sealed runs") }}
            <span class="row-id">Mean checkpoint completion of the sealed runs</span>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Continuity</td>
          <td>
            {{ continuity.continuity_formatted }}
            <span class="row-id">
              ({{ continuity.runs_completed }} × {{ continuity.coverage_mean | show("0") }}) ÷ {{ continuity.runs_expected }}
            </span>
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>Runs missing</h3>

    <p class="gap-count">
      {{ continuity.runs_missing | length }} scheduled run{{ "" if continuity.runs_missing | length == 1 else "s" }}
      with no seal, on {{ continuity_missing | length }} day{{ "" if continuity_missing | length == 1 else "s" }}.
    </p>

    {% if continuity_missing %}
      <table class="data-table continuity-missing">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Date</th>
            <th class="figure">Runs missing</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for row in continuity_missing %}
            <tr>
              <td>{{ row.date }}</td>
              <td class="figure">{{ row.runs }}</td>
            </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    {% else %}
      <p class="absent-note">
        Every day in the window has the runs the schedule expects.
      </p>
    {% endif %}

    <h3>Seals and chain</h3>

    <p class="lede">
      Each counted run's seal checked against its record, evidence and outputs
      as they are now. Continuity and the chain are separate claims: a complete
      set of runs with a broken chain is not the same as a sparse set with an
      intact one.
    </p>

    {% set unchecked = continuity.runs_completed - continuity.seals_verified - continuity.seals_broken %}
    <table class="data-table continuity-seals">
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Seals verified</td>
          <td class="figure">{{ continuity.seals_verified }}</td>
          <td><span class="row-id">Every check passed</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Seals broken</td>
          <td class="figure">{{ continuity.seals_broken }}</td>
          <td><span class="row-id">At least one check failed</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Could not verify</td>
          <td class="figure">{{ unchecked }}</td>
          <td><span class="row-id">No check failed, but at least one could not be made</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Chain</td>
          <td class="figure">{{ "Intact" if continuity.chain_intact else "Not intact" }}</td>
          <td><span class="row-id">Intact only when every counted seal's link to the one before it was checked and holds</span></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

  {% else %}
    <p class="absent-note">
      No continuity was worked out: {{ no_continuity | show("no route folder was found") }}.
    </p>
  {% endif %}

</section>
